{"id":"def:propensity-rate-regimes","name":"Generic and primitive propensity-rate regimes","construction":"Fix before observing data a jointly measurable learner rule on every training complement and a deterministic sequence \(r_{\pi,n}\to0\). The generic maintained learner condition is
\[
\lim_{M\to\infty}\limsup_{n\to\infty}\sup_{\mathbf P\in\mathscr P}
P_n\!\left(\max_k\lVert\bar\pi_{-k,n}-\pi_n\rVert_{L^2(P_{X,n})}>Mr_{\pi,n}\right)=0.
\]
This is an estimator-side hypothesis and does not define membership in \(\mathscr P\). For the primitive H\"older regime, let \(\mathfrak G_{J}\) be a deterministic finite \(L^\infty\)-net of \(\{g\in\Sigma(t_\pi,L_\pi;\mathcal X):\varepsilon\le g\le1-\varepsilon\}\), with mesh \(2^{-Jt_\pi}\) and \(\log|\mathfrak G_J|\lesssim2^{Jd_X}\). On each training complement choose the lexicographically first minimizer of \(\sum_j(A_{j,n}-g(X_{j,n}))^2\) over \(g\in\mathfrak G_J\), and clip it to \([\varepsilon,1-\varepsilon]\), with \(2^{Jd_X}\asymp n^{d_X/(2t_\pi+d_X)}\).","inputs":["\(\mathcal T_{-k,n}\)","\( ar\pi_{-k,n}\)","\(r_{\pi,n}\)","\(arepsilon\)"]}
